From d60df40dfc6cd442e28fee60e226e0796d9e1b01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Holdren <Dylan@UniversalBasicInc.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:17:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Run neural network potentials on Intel GPUs through LibTorch
 XPU

The NNPot interface selected the inference device by asking the CUDA or
HIP runtime for its current device, so a SYCL build for Intel GPUs always
ran the model on the CPU. mdrun now passes the DeviceInformation of the
device assigned to the rank to the MD modules through the simulation
setup notifier, and TorchModel matches that device against the devices
LibTorch enumerates to run on the same Intel GPU (torch::kXPU).

CMake detects whether the LibTorch found has XPU support (the torch_xpu
target), warns when a SYCL build pairs with a LibTorch that lacks it, and
checks that the LibTorch headers compile with the configured C++ standard,
since PyTorch 2.14 and later require C++20.

The NNPot unit tests now also run the GPU cases on Intel devices.

Refs #PLACEHOLDER

Signed-off-by: Dylan Holdren <Dylan@UniversalBasicInc.com>
